r Chase Anniversary DIPA</span></span></strong><span><span> with Mosaic, Citra, Cashmere &amp; Talus<br>• </span></span><strong><span><span>Vasen Alpenglow </span></span></strong><span><span>Hazy IPA</span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Ocelot Wilderness of False Flowers</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> IPA with Simcoe, Strata &amp; Elani</span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/43f36c7d-27b9-6d75-a3a3-094759c2f8df.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f31e/72.png\" alt=\"🌞\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"> </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Grimm</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> with that natural glow<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Day of Radiance</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Hazy IPA with Luminosa &amp; Citra<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Canopy Door</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Hazy DIPA with Enigma, El Dorado, Simcoe &amp; Citra</span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/15837cf4-8bf5-eb10-fb96-f6b512e31661.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1f3b8/72.png\" alt=\"🎸\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></span></span></span><span> Fresh hops from</span></span><strong><span><span> The Veil</span></span></strong><span><span><br>• </span></span><strong><span><span>Shreddy Krueger</span></span></strong><span><span> West Coast IPA with Mosaic<br>•</span></span><strong><span><span> Premium Sauce</span></span></strong><span><span> Hazy IPA with Galaxy, Mosaic &amp; BRU-1</span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/7663fe02-83e4-6718-9d53-a108808cc450.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><img src=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/e/notoemoji/17.0/1fabb/72.png\" alt=\"🪻\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">Local love</span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span><span>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Potter’s Cranberry Orange Blossom</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> cider</span></span></span></span><span><span><span><br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Silver Branch Sun Runner</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span> Witbier<br>• </span></span></span><strong><span><span><span>Bingo Fest Friends </span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>Festbier</span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<div class=\"reader-image-row reader-brew-grid\" data-columns=\"2\"><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/52de3c22-2546-b83a-cc85-ecbde8976844.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><span><span><span><span>🍾 Poppin bottles<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Bell’s Expedition</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> Russian Imperial Stout<br>• </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Maine Beer Lunch</span></span></span></span></strong><span><span><span><span> IPA returns!</span></span></span></span></p></figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/6aab1405-e798-13c3-9520-9426a21ac015.jpeg\" width=\"298\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><p><strong><span>Prost pack #4!</span></strong><span><span><span><span>Mixed pack of Oktoberfest brews: </span></span></span></span><strong><span><span><span><span>Notch Festbier, Port City Oktoberfest, Jack's Abby Copper Legend, Brooklyn Oktoberfest, Three Floyds Munsterfest &amp; Destihl Oktoberfest</span></span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p><span>Bluejacket Reflections Festbier</span></p>\n<p><span>Fine Creek Circus of Puffins West Coast IPA</span></p></figcaption></figure></div>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/577ea500-3045-ac51-ac72-b0ad9970b9e6.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span>Macanita MAC Tinto: </span></strong><span><span><span><span>Known as a bit of a mover-shaker in the Portuguese winemaking world, Joana Maçanita reminds us why we're obsessed with reds from the Douro Valley. Coming from high altitude vineyards and finishing in both concrete and stainless (rather than oak), MAC Tinto is big on flavor, but not on weight with ripe black fruit, dried herbs and a mineral finish. Pairs beautifully with grilled and smoked meat. Native Yeast.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><strong><span><span><span>Poggio Le Volpi Roma Rosso</span></span></span></strong><span><span><span>: </span></span></span><span><span><span><span>It's back! Our friend Michelle is always looking for our best \"dirty\" wine. Next up on her drinking list is modern-Rome blend from Lazio, Italy. Basically a Roman God in a glass - robust and earthy with loads of rich dark fruit, leather and licorice.</span></span></span></span></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/dd0ec982-c24d-10b0-c848-133bb28ed64b.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p><strong><span><span><span><span>A Graves Bordeaux? </span></span></span></span></strong><em><strong><span><span><span><span>Bordeaux-n’t</span></span></span></span></strong></em><strong><span><span><span><span> Mind if I Do!</span></span></span></span></strong></p>\n<p><span><span><span><span>As “false fall” creeps into the DMV, I’m seeking wine with a little more bite and body–something that’s going to warm me up a little after a walk in the crisp evening air or alongside a charcuterie plate as I’m curled up on the couch with the latest episode of The Great British Bake Off.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span><span>Enter Chateau Trebiac’s Graves Bordeaux. This gorgeous, leggy red blend fits the bill perfectly, offering an easy warmth and well-rounded palate that’s sure to please those who usually steer clear of drier reds.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span><span>Winemaker Arnaud de Butler said “au revoir” to Paris and settled in about 35 kilometers south of Bordeaux, learning about wine under the tutelage of his father. This completely rehabilitated vineyard is situated on a gravel plateau, which allows the Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot grapes to develop deep, rich fruit flavors without sacrificing structure.Thicker skins also lend to a gentler, more mellow tannin profile.&nbsp;</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span><span><span><span>On the nose, this wine’s full of notes of blackberries and red fruit, followed by a hint of toasty hazelnut, chocolate, and warm spices.&nbsp;Serve her straight out of the bottle with a grilled steak (take advantage of patio weather while you can!), a spaghetti bolognese or all’assassina, or a nice chunk of gouda. Or, if you’re me, pair your Bake Off watch with Nigella Lawson’s </span></span></span></span><a href=\"https://us.list-manage.com/5NdHbfeI6UN?e=01c6cdb4b7&amp;c2id=78b36ba273cb71acbb53a8fce08ea4f0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span><span><span><span><span>Chocolate Olive Oil Cake</span></span></span></span></span></a><span><span><span><span>. Cheers!</span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><em><span><span><span><span>This week’s writeup is brought to you by Erika</span></span></span></span></em></p>\n<img src=\"https://mcusercontent.com/be20bbfba341582993786f7f0/images/44528625-75ce-77b6-246b-4628384a151b.jpeg\" width=\"612\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n<p>Thanks for your business! See you soon, Beth, Julie &amp; Aidan and the entire Brew Crew</p>",
